For Test 2 (stepped-wedge cluster randomized trial):

· Number of sites: 6
· Number of periods: 4
· Individuals per site per period: 20
· Total sample size: 6 × 4 × 20 = 480
· Intra-cluster correlation (ICC): 0.05
· Design effect: 1 + (20 - 1) × 0.05 = 1.95
· Effective sample size: 480 / 1.95 = 246
· Minimum detectable effect: 15% reduction in time-to-stabilization
· Power: 80%
· Significance level: 0.05

This calculation uses the standard formula for stepped-wedge designs. The ICC of 0.05 is conservative for homeless services research, where clustering is typically weak because individuals within a site have heterogeneous trajectories.

F.7 Pre-Registration Requirements

The following must be pre-registered before data collection:

· Primary and secondary outcomes
· Analysis plan (including subgroup analyses)
· Sample size and power calculations
· Stopping rules
· Handling of missing data
· Ethical approvals

Registration will be on ClinicalTrials.gov or an equivalent registry. Pre-registration prevents post-hoc revision of hypotheses and strengthens the credibility of the evaluation.

